  "description": "Capability for the main Blue Environment window — grants access to all custom Rust commands and required core plugin permissions. NOTE: this file previously had a duplicate, malformed override (\"core:default\" shadowed by an empty-allow-list duplicate) that broke IPC app-wide; if commands break app-wide again, check for a duplicate identifier with a narrower \"allow\" list shadowing the real grant before assuming a webview-scoping issue. Every one of this app's custom commands also needs an explicit allow-<command> permission here (Tauri's ACL denies anything not listed) — this is NOT hand-maintained: it is generated, together with build.rs's command list, by scripts/gen-tauri-allowlist.mjs from the single source of truth, main.rs's generate_handler![...] list. Run `node scripts/gen-tauri-allowlist.mjs` (or `npm run gen:allowlist`) after adding, removing, or renaming any #[tauri::command] in the handler list — do not hand-edit the allow-* entries below, they will be overwritten. `npm run gen:allowlist:check` (wired into CI) fails the build if this file has drifted from main.rs.",
